In article <1797@yenta.alb.nm.us> dt@yenta.alb.nm.us (David B. Thomas) writes:
>5. I killed a cockatrice and kept the corpse, figuring I could wield it
>if I got into trouble.  Not wanting to touch it carelessly, I put it in
>my bag.  Later, when I went to take it out, everything seemed fine:
>Do you want to take something out? y [...] (i) a cockatrice corpse
>Great!  But immediately I did an inventory and it had vanished.  I mean it.
>I think that is definitely a bug.

I'll bet this is the problem here:  Whenever you kill a monster, the corpse
will only last for a certain amount of time before it rots totally away.
This is checked for all corpses lying on the ground, and in your inventory.
It is probably not checked for corpses in a bag of holding.  Probably this
time had already expired, so when you pulled the corpse from the bag, it
immediately checked the timestamp on the corpse, discovered that it should
already have rotted away, and simply removed it from your inventory.  

Try picking up a corpse and just keeping it in your inventory.  Eventually
it will just disappear.

